---
import { ASANA, PATHS, SELF_HOSTING_FACTS } from '@lib/compare/asana-alternative';
---

<section id="aa-deploy" class="border-t border-line" aria-labelledby="aa-deploy-title">
  <div class="wrap py-16 md:py-24 grid lg:grid-cols-12 gap-10 lg:gap-12">
    <div class="lg:col-span-5">
      <h2 id="aa-deploy-title" class="h2">
        Can we run it ourselves?
      </h2>
      <p class="prose mt-5">
        Yes, and it is a real commitment. Nothing Left is open source under AGPL-3.0, and the hosted beta runs the same
        build. Running it yourself means the infrastructure and its maintenance are your team’s responsibility, not
        ours. The guides cover Docker Compose on one machine and AWS.
      </p>
      <p class="prose mt-4">
        Asana is a cloud service; its pricing page says it does not plan to offer an internally hosted version.{' '}
        <a class="link font-normal" href={ASANA.pricing} rel="noopener">
          Asana pricing FAQ
          <span class="arr ext" aria-hidden="true">
            ↗
          </span>
        </a>
      </p>
      <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-6 gap-y-3">
        <a class="link text-sm" href={PATHS.selfHosting}>
          Self-hosting in detail
          <span class="arr" aria-hidden="true">
            →
          </span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <dl class="lg:col-span-6 lg:col-start-7 rule-list">
      {SELF_HOSTING_FACTS.map(fact => (
        <div class="py-5">
          <dt class="text-sm font-medium">{fact.title}</dt>
          <dd class="prose text-base mt-1">{fact.body}</dd>
        </div>
      ))}
    </dl>
  </div>
</section>
